  "lastName": "Su",
  "overview": "I am an assistant professor in Department of Genetics. I have long-standing interests in epigenetics that regulate gene expression without altering the DNA sequences. Such epigenetic mechanisms are important for human development and health, especially due to its dynamic interactions with the environmental factors and microenvironmental cues. My lab uses a combination of genomics experiments and dry-lab bioinformatics to study epitranscriptomics (RNA modifications) in human health. We are a new lab and currently recruiting at all levels. Please check out our lab website here: https://www.sulabrna.com",
